research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-9758-  "quote": "Let $F$ be an ordered field, with field structure as in [[def-field]], and for $n \\ge 1$ let $n \\cdot 1_F$ denote the canonical natural number $\\underbrace{1_F + \\cdots + 1_F}_{n}$, defined recursively by $1 \\cdot 1_F = 1_F$ and $(n+1) \\cdot 1_F = n \\cdot 1_F + 1_F$. Then for every $n \\ge 1$: - $n \\cdot 1_F > 0$ and $(n+1) \\cdot 1_F > n \\cdot 1_F$; - the map $n \\mapsto n \\cdot 1_F$ is strictly increasing, hence injective, on $\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}$; - $(m+n) \\cdot 1_F = m \\cdot 1_F + n \\cdot 1_F$ and $(mn) \\cdot 1_F = (m \\cdot 1_F)(n \\cdot 1_F)$ for all $m, n \\ge 1$.",
